! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F209D "TESTS OF
! INDICATORS" for ADD DOUBLE TO MAGNITUDE, sub-tests D6-D9
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.107, octal 015652.00-015670.00,
! where the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0" begins): the Lost
! Significance indicator, the half of F209D that D1-D5 left behind.
!
! Each sub-test clears LS with BLSZ, runs one add, and asks once:
!
!   D6  LS on   DL(U) FPK31 with FPK32's fraction dropped into the low
!               half by C0011, then D-MG(U) FPK32 -- a cancelling
!               subtract, so the result fraction goes to zero
!   D7  LS off  DL(U) FPK0 + D+MG(U) FPK0 -- zero plus zero
!   D8  LS on   DL(U) FPK21 with FPK41's fraction in the low half,
!               then D+MG(U) FPK42
!   D9  LS off  DL(U) FK35 + D+MG(U) FK38, the flagged path (FK35 has
!               EF=1); the listing notes "result contains propagated
!               EF+1"
!
! D7 is the one that bears directly on the model. It is the printed
! source of the exception clause in the F208D5 LS fix: a zero result
! sets LS only when the operands were not BOTH zero. Zero plus zero
! is a zero result whose significance was never lost, and F209D7 is
! the listing asking exactly that. D9 is the first LS question put to
! the flagged path, where fpAddDouble returns a survivor whole.
!
! Transcribed as printed: D8's header comment reads "LS INDICATOR OFF"
! but its one question is BZLS, "error if LS ind off" -- so the test
! requires LS ON and the header contradicts it. The encodings are
! unambiguous (1304.15 40 is BZLS, against 1304.15 42 for BLS), so
! this is the listing's own inconsistency, the same class as D1's
! BRGZ-labelled-RZ. Transcribed as the encoding column reads.
!
! New encoding ground: BLSZ (1304.15 46 / 15653.15 46) is the first
! branch-on-indicator in this series with both the clear and the
! branch-on bits set. BZLS is 40 and BLS is 42, as in D1-D5's family;
! 46 is a combination nothing before this block reached.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pools p.176. PASS sits at 015670.00, on the routine's exit.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), C0011, D+MG(U), D-MG(U), SIC, and the three
! LS branches BLSZ, BZLS and BLS.
! verify_fp_arith_f209d6_9_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)022044.0
FPK31   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000000000000000000
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022056.0
FPK41   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001040000000000000000
FPK42   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001460000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022205.0
FK35    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777400000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022210.0
FK38    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0777572525252525252520

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15652.0
FADM6   B, $+.32                         ! F209D6: LS indicator on
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20
        D-MG(U), FPK32
        SIC, SEN
        BZLS, SERS                       ! error if LS indicator not on
        B, $+.32                         ! F209D7: LS indicator off
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK0
        D+MG(U), FPK0
        SIC, SEN
        BLS, SERS                        ! error if LS indicator on
        B, $+.32                         ! F209D8: printed "LS INDICATOR OFF"
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK21
        C0011(BU,48), FPK41+.12, 20
        D+MG(U), FPK42
        SIC, SEN
        BZLS, SERS                       ! error if LS ind off
        B, $+.32                         ! F209D9: test LS ind., off condition
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FK35
        D+MG(U), FK38                    ! result contains propagated EF+1
        SIC, SEN
        BLS, SERS                        ! error if LS indicator on
PASS    BEW, $                   ! 015670.00: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, FADM6
